id: sense
name: Sense
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
clashSkill: clairvoyance
clashDefenderSkills: concealment
sense: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Lock on to an Opponent's energy. A Clash of your Clairvoyance against their
  Concealment, and winning reads how many Holding Back Stacks they are carrying - told
  to you rather than to the table, since the whole of what it buys is knowing.
text: >
  Sense Maneuver [1/Round]: Lock on to the energy of an opponent.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent. Make a Skill Clash (Clairvoyance vs Concealment) against
  them. If you win, you can tell how many stacks of Holding Back they possess and if
  they are currently in their Transformation with the highest Tier of Power Requirement
  (you do not know which Transformation they possess – you just have a general feeling
  whether or not they are still holding back their full power).

---

# --- The Clash ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "(Clairvoyance vs Concealment)", and one Skill each side - so nobody is asked which,
# where the Feint's "(Bluff vs Intuition/Perception)" asks the defender.
#
# Worth noticing what the pairing does: Concealment is the Skill the Holding Back
# Maneuver's own stacks improve, by 1 each to a maximum of 3. So the thing being looked
# for is what makes it harder to find, which is the one place in these rules where a
# Resource defends itself.
#
# A tie goes to the Defender, here as everywhere else.
#
# No script. Winning reads two things off somebody else and writes nothing anywhere -
# the first Maneuver in this system whose whole effect is that one person now knows
# something - and a passive writes Slots onto the character holding it.
#
# --- The half that can be answered -------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You can tell how many stacks of Holding Back they possess." A Resource with a count,
# read off the target and stated as a number.
#
# --- The half that cannot ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "And if they are currently in their Transformation with the highest Tier of Power
# Requirement."
#
# There are no Transformations in this system. Not "none built for this Maneuver" - none
# at all: `traits/` has no transformations directory, nothing records which Transformation
# a character is in, and no entry anywhere gives one a Tier of Power Requirement to be the
# highest of. The kind exists in the Trait loader and in the Slots table, waiting for a
# file.
#
# So this half is put on the card as the question it is, for the table to answer, rather
# than guessed at from the Tier of Power - which is the number a Transformation would
# raise and is not the same thing as being in one. The day Transformations exist, what
# changes here is one sentence of the reading.
#
# --- Told to one side ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The reading is whispered: whoever owns the sensing character, and every GM. Everything
# else a settled Clash leaves behind goes out in front of everybody, because it is a thing
# that happened - somebody knocked Prone is knocked Prone at the table.
#
# This is not that, and it is not the reading the private-breakdown rule declined either.
# There, a roll's workings are hidden as a courtesy and the total still reaches the table,
# because the total is what the table is waiting for. Here the answer IS what the Maneuver
# buys, and reading it out hands it to exactly the people the entry is keeping it from.
# The entry is careful about how little is learned even by the one who paid for it - "you
# do not know which Transformation they possess" - and a public note would tell the rest
# of the room more than that.
#
# What the table does see is that it landed, which is not a secret: both sides rolled in
# public and the card already says who won.
#
# Losing is said out loud. Nothing private happened.
#
# --- What is not built ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system, which the Arrogant Declaration,
# Analysis, Hype, Brace, Flip and Holding Back files all say about their own Minion lines.
#
# "Target an Opponent" with no range on it, so there is no distance to police - and this
# system measures none anyway.
#
# --- How it is gained ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not known. Clairvoyance is a Required Skill and its entry has not been given, so no
# Skill in the table opens this yet - it is the seventh Special Maneuver reachable only
# through an effect that grants it, alongside Attack Absorption, Dirty Trick, Insult,
# Internal Attack, Liquid Form and Power Drain.
#
# Clairvoyance is the obvious guess, and the guess is worth nothing: the Dirty Trick is a
# Clash made with Bluff and Bluff opens the Feint instead. Being the Skill a Maneuver rolls
# and being the Skill that hands it over are two different questions, and only the Skill's
# own entry answers the second.
